course: dictionary
lesson: 6535
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word neuter is a good example. «A good home gives a kitten a clean tray, a tall steady post, and indoor life until it is vaccinated, neutered and old enough.» Here neutered is something a vet does to a pet, so it means the small operation that stops it having kittens.
explain: The same word can also be a grammar label. «Ukrainian nouns have grammatical gender, a grammar label, not boy or girl: "вікно" (window) is neuter.» Nothing is being done to a window. Here neuter is a label that says the word is neither masculine nor feminine.
explain: Always ask: what is the sentence about? A pet, a word, or a bee? Then try your chosen meaning in the sentence and check it still makes sense. If the talk is about a pet, the vet meaning fits. If it is about nouns, the grammar meaning fits.
fact: Neuter is an adjective, and it is also a verb: to neuter, neuters, neutered, neutering.
fact: «Neuter» can mean to have a vet operate on a pet so it cannot have babies.
fact: «Neuter» in grammar means neither masculine nor feminine. German, Latin and Ukrainian all have neuter nouns.
fact: «Altered» (US) and «seen to» (UK) are other ways people say that a pet has been neutered.
fact: «Neuter» can also mean having no sex organs, like worker bees.
exercise: «Kittens stay inside until they are vaccinated, neutered and old enough.» What does neutered mean here? | *Had a small operation so the cat cannot have kittens | Given a new name | Taught to climb tall posts | Sent to live outside
exercise: «Ukrainian nouns have grammatical gender.» In grammar, what does neuter mean? | Very old | Made from metal | *Neither masculine nor feminine | Both masculine and feminine
exercise: Lena says worker bees are neuter. What does neuter mean for worker bees? | *They have no sex organs | They can only sing | They live in houses | They are very large
test: Ella reads, «Seen to means a pet has been neutered.» What does seen to mean in that sentence? | A pet has been lost | A pet has been checked by the teacher | A pet has been fed | *A pet has had a small operation so it cannot have kittens
test: Noah reads that "вікно" (window) is neuter. Which meaning of neuter is used? | *Grammar: neither masculine nor feminine | Very old | Pet operation so it cannot have babies | Giving out light
exam: Which meaning fits «Kittens stay inside until they are vaccinated and neutered»? | *A vet's operation so a pet cannot have kittens | Worker bee with no sex organs | Grammar label for nouns
